    ("Data Preprocessing", "Why might simply deleting all rows with any missing values (listwise deletion) be problematic for some datasets?", "If missing values aren't random, this can introduce bias and also discard potentially large amounts of otherwise-useful data", "This approach always improves data quality with no downsides", "Missing values never affect statistical analysis", "This is the only valid approach to handling missing data", "A", "If the pattern of missingness is related to other variables (not purely random), deleting those rows can bias the remaining dataset, and it can also waste a substantial amount of otherwise valid information in other columns of those rows."),
    ("Overfitting", "Why does increasing model complexity (e.g. more parameters) without a corresponding increase in training data often increase the risk of overfitting?", "A more complex model has greater capacity to fit not just the underlying patterns but also the noise and idiosyncrasies specific to the limited training set", "More parameters always reduce overfitting risk regardless of data size", "Model complexity has no relationship to overfitting", "Overfitting can only occur with very simple models", "A", "A model with more capacity (parameters) can fit increasingly intricate patterns in a fixed-size training set, including noise and coincidental quirks that don't reflect genuine, generalizable structure."),
