    ("Underfitting", "Why might an underfitting model show similar (low) performance on both very different training set sizes?", "Because the model's capacity is fundamentally too limited to capture the underlying patterns, so adding more of the same kind of data doesn't help it fit better", "Underfitting only occurs with very large datasets", "An underfitting model's performance always improves dramatically regardless of the data added", "This scenario indicates the model is actually overfitting", "A", "If a model's capacity is inherently too limited to represent the underlying relationship (e.g. a linear model for a strongly non-linear pattern), simply adding more data of the same kind won't help it fit any better."),
