    ("Evaluation Metrics", "In a medical screening scenario where missing a true positive (a sick patient) is far more costly than a false alarm, which metric would typically be prioritized, and why?", "Recall, because it measures how many actual positive cases were correctly identified, directly addressing the cost of missed detections", "Precision, because it never considers missed positive cases", "Accuracy alone, since it is unaffected by class imbalance in this scenario", "Training time, since faster models are always preferred regardless of accuracy", "A", "Since missing a true positive is especially costly here, recall (which measures how many actual positives were correctly caught) becomes the priority metric, even if it means tolerating more false positives."),
