    ("Evaluation Metrics", "Why can relying solely on the R-squared value be misleading when evaluating a regression model's quality?", "A high R-squared doesn't guarantee the model is well-specified or free from overfitting, and it can be artificially inflated by simply adding more features, even irrelevant ones", "R-squared always perfectly reflects a model's true predictive power with no caveats", "R-squared cannot be computed for any regression model", "R-squared is only relevant for classification tasks", "A", "R-squared tends to increase (or at least not decrease) simply by adding more features, even irrelevant ones, which can create a misleadingly optimistic picture of model quality without considering overfitting or model simplicity."),
